# A register that is right

`set aside` is a rule read to its end and accepted as it stands.

`repair owed` is a rule whose pattern is to be changed in this tree.

## cs/example-first, set aside

The set is read rather than pasted:

```
gh api "repos/owner/repository/code-scanning/alerts?state=open&per_page=100" \
  --paginate --jq '.[] | .rule.id' | sort | uniq -c
```

## cs/example-second, repair owed

A search this tree answers:

```
git grep -n 'Code-scanning rules' -- docs/code-scanning-dispositions.md
```
